3. The /connect system
3.1 What it does
Every QR code on every USRad business card routes to usrad.com/connect. That page does exactly one thing: it asks the visitor who they are, then sends them to the right place.
The page is deliberately small. It is a routing layer, not a destination. The destination is whatever existing canonical landing page best matches the visitor's audience type. /connect's job is to make sure that handoff happens within fifteen seconds of the scan.
