Why payor routes to /partner
USRad is itself the payor to imaging providers. Health plans are not customers — they are potential partnership counterparties. The /partner page already handles partner segmentation; we added "Health Plans & Payors" as a first-class category there so payor visitors find themselves named.
3.3 The page flow
There are two layers to the system, both intentionally short:
Layer 1 — /connect (the picker)
    • Navy hero band with USRad wordmark, gold accent rule, and the brand statement verbatim from the card
    • One-sentence prompt: "Tell us who you are and we'll point you to what's most relevant."
    • Six tappable cards in a single-column mobile / 2-column desktop grid
    • Each card shows the audience label plus a one-line sub-label so identification is unambiguous
Layer 2 — /connect/[audience] (the bridge)
    • Same navy hero band so visual continuity holds across the transition
    • A short acknowledgment ("Welcome. You're looking at USRad as…") that confirms the visitor was seen
    • A one-paragraph value proposition specific to that audience
    • A proof line (where applicable) that grounds USRad's credibility — usually the AnciCare PPO history
    • One primary CTA button leading to the canonical landing page
    • A small "That's not me — show me the options" back link
Total time on /connect plus /connect/[audience] before the visitor reaches a substantive landing page: under thirty seconds for a focused reader.
4. How it was built
4.1 Technical stack
The /connect system lives inside the existing usrad.com Astro 5.7.4 SSR application deployed on Vercel. It uses CarbonLayout (the primary marketing layout), Tailwind CSS, and the brand's design tokens. No new dependencies were added.
