4.3 The data file pattern
All copy for all six audiences lives in one TypeScript file: connectAudiences.ts. Each audience is a typed object containing its picker label, sub-label, page headline, acknowledgment, body paragraph, proof line, and CTA configuration.
How to update copy
All audience copy is in src/data/connectAudiences.ts. Editing that one file updates both the picker labels on /connect and the page copy on /connect/[audience]. No template editing required.
4.4 The CarbonLayout enhancement
CarbonLayout previously had no mechanism for pages to inject content into <head>. This caused a workaround during /connect development: noindex was being injected via inline JavaScript after page load, which is fragile and crawler-visible only after JS execution.
As part of this work, CarbonLayout received a named slot at the end of <head>:
<slot name="head" />
Any page using CarbonLayout can now inject head content cleanly. The /connect pages use this for both robots noindex and canonical URLs. Other pages on the site can adopt the same pattern when needed (page-specific OG tags, JSON-LD, hreflang, and so on).
